Title: THE GLASS KEY
Author: Helen Voss
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. ASHWORTH MANOR - LIBRARY - DAY

Rain on leaded glass. DETECTIVE MAYA QUINN, 45, examines an empty velvet case. MRS. ASHWORTH, 70s, trembles in a wingback chair.
MAYA
The GLASS KEY was here at midnight. Who had access after dinner?
MRS. ASHWORTH
Only family. And the boy who tends the garden.

INT. MANOR - GREENHOUSE - DAY

Quinn interviews TOMAS, 22, gardener, mud on his boots. A silver locket peeks from his shirt.
TOMAS
I lock up at nine. I don't touch the old woman's trinkets.
MAYA
Trinket opens a wall safe in this house. Try again.

INT. MANOR - NORTH WING HALL - DAY

Quinn finds fresh scratches around a portrait of the late MR. ASHWORTH. The frame sits crooked.
Behind the portrait: a narrow door, slightly ajar. Cold air slips through.

INT. HIDDEN STUDY - DAY

Dusty ledgers. A GLASS KEY replica on the desk — obvious decoy. A note in elegant script: For the one who asks the right question.
MAYA
Someone wanted us to look behind the painting.

INT. MANOR - LIBRARY - DAY

Quinn reassembles the room. Mrs. Ashworth pales as Maya holds up the decoy and the real case side by side.
MAYA
The key didn't leave the manor. It was moved to tell a story. Whose story, Mrs. Ashworth?

FADE OUT.


THE END
